# Product update notices

When we introduce user-facing changes (new screens, filters, billing copy, account tools, or behavior customers will notice), do not stop at the code.

Also draft copy for **Platform admin → Maintenance & product notices → New product update**.

Fill:

- **Type:** Product update / what's new (not maintenance, no downtime)
- **Title:** short, customer-facing (often keep “What's new in CasinFreight”)
- **Popup message:** a short list of what changed, in CasinFreight voice — plain English, Philippine ops, no git/commit jargon, no Firestore/rules/deploy talk
- **Show popup until:** about 7 days from today unless the user picks another date
- **Active:** checked

Only include features that actually landed (or that the user is about to publish). Skip internal-only work.

Put the ready-to-paste title and message in the reply so the owner can publish without rewriting.
